#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:3
msgid "Tool manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:5
msgid ""
"Declare a set of pipx tools in one file and install, upgrade, or prune them "
"as a unit with ``pipx manifest``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:9
msgid "Write the manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:11
msgid ""
"The manifest is a ``pipx.toml`` file. Each dependency group holds one `PEP "
"508 <https://peps.python.org/pep-0508/>`__ package requirement and names its "
"pipx environment. ``project.dependencies`` must be an empty list so each "
"group resolves on its own; pipx rejects the manifest otherwise:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:15
msgid ""
"[project]\n"
"name = \"pipx-tools\"\n"
"version = \"1\"\n"
"dependencies = []\n"
"requires-python = \">=3.10\"\n"
"\n"
"[dependency-groups]\n"
"black = [\"black>=25,<26\"]\n"
"httpie = [\"httpie\"]\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx]\n"
"version = \"1.0\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx.tools.black]\n"
"apps = [\"black\"]\n"
"lock = \"pylock.black.toml\"\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx.tools.httpie]\n"
"apps = [\"http\", \"https\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:37
msgid ""
"Add a ``tool.pipx.tools`` table only when a tool needs policy beyond its "
"package requirement. A tool table may set ``suffix``, ``apps``, ``include-"
"dependencies``, ``include-resources-from``, ``expose``, or ``lock``. Use "
"``include-resources-from = [\"PACKAGE\"]`` to select dependency resources; "
"do not combine it with ``include-dependencies``. Relative ``lock`` paths "
"start from the manifest directory. Put `nab <https://pypi.org/project/nab/"
">`__ settings in ``tool.nab``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:43
msgid ""
"Use the normalized package name plus its suffix as the environment name when "
"a tool sets a suffix:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:45
msgid ""
"[dependency-groups]\n"
"black-24 = [\"black==24.10.0\"]\n"
"\n"
"[tool.pipx.tools.black-24]\n"
"suffix = \"-24\"\n"
"apps = [\"black\"]"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:54
msgid "Package requirements use PEP 508 syntax without environment markers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:58
msgid "Lock the manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:60
msgid ""
"``nab`` resolves each locked dependency group into a `PEP 751 <https://"
"peps.python.org/pep-0751/>`__ lock file. Install it, then generate the "
"declared locks:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:63
msgid ""
"$ pipx install nab\n"
"$ pipx manifest lock ./pipx.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:68
msgid ""
"``pipx manifest lock`` passes the manifest to ``nab`` once per locked "
"dependency group, and records that group as the lock's default so installers "
"select it. Existing locks seed their replacements, and pipx overwrites the "
"declared files only after every resolution succeeds. Entries without "
"``lock`` stay unlocked. ``pipx manifest lock`` refuses to run when a "
"``lock`` path resolves outside the manifest directory, through ``..``, "
"``~``, an absolute path, or a symlink; ``pipx manifest sync`` still reads "
"locks kept elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:76
msgid "Apply the manifest"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:78
msgid "$ pipx manifest sync ./pipx.toml"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:82
msgid ""
"``sync`` installs, upgrades, or downgrades each declared tool. The backend "
"resolves unlocked specs on each run; locked entries install from the "
"artifacts in their named PEP 751 files. Under the `pip <https://pip.pypa.io/"
">`__ backend, a locked entry needs pip 26.1 or newer; run ``pipx upgrade-"
"shared`` when pipx reports an older one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:86
msgid ""
"pipx restores an existing environment and its exposed resources when a tool "
"fails to install, lacks a required app, or the sync is interrupted. For an "
"environment that already exists, ``sync`` keeps the installer and venv "
"options recorded at install time, such as ``--index-url`` or ``--system-site-"
"packages``, the same way ``pipx reinstall`` does, and keeps the apps, manual "
"pages, and completions of its injected packages exposed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:91
msgid ""
"Pass ``--prune`` to uninstall environments absent from the manifest. pipx "
"skips pruning when any declared tool fails to sync:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:94
msgid "$ pipx manifest sync ./pipx.toml --prune"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:98
msgid ""
"Without ``--prune``, sync leaves your other pipx environments alone. Pass "
"``--global`` (not available on Windows) or ``--backend`` after ``sync`` to "
"select the pipx store or the installation backend. pipx reads only the "
"manifest path you supply on the command line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:104
msgid "Verify it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:106
msgid "$ pipx list --short"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../how-to/tool-manifest.rst:110
msgid "Each declared tool appears at the version its group resolved to."
msgstr ""
